# S38-S41-horplus: the hall at 16:9 in horizontal plus: the 4:3 view's height, wider.
#
# S38 is under V3-35a, "id spread its ninety degrees across any width. On a wide screen,
# that cuts off the top and the bottom."; S39 under V3-35b, "Horizontal plus keeps the
# height, and adds world at the sides."
#
# Assembly: S38 is S38-S41-4x3 shown 1440x1080 (area-averaged) in the frame's centre to
# file second 4.5; from 3.0, rust lines mark where id's 16:9 cuts it (it keeps the central
# three quarters of the rows) and the rows beyond dim; over 4.5 to 6.0 (smoothstep) the
# picture grows to 1920x1440, cut to the frame, so the lines ride out to its edges; late
# in that growth it settles onto S38-S41-id (the same picture). S39 cross-fades S38-S41-id
# to S38-S41-horplus between film seconds 9.3 and 10.3 (smoothstep), then a bronze outline
# of the 4:3 box fades in from 10.6. S38 is the master's frames 0 to 617, S39 498 to 965.

map e1m5

duration 24
fps 60
size 1920x1080
frames 498..966

preset slop
hud off
cvar gamma 0.8
cvar fov_adapt 1

camera path
key 0   -1536,1423.91,200  0,90  ease linear
key 24  -1536,1618.09,200  0,90

events on
